			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Update formatting exclusions for Element package configurations\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "981ef5e9b12b1bce8ef8f1bfca1ea5ca83785470"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:15:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Advance Element submodule with dispatcher extraction and runtime fixes\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to a74c89e5, pulling in a coordinated commit spanning Cocoon, Mountain, and Worker that extracts large inline match blocks into dedicated modules and addresses three runtime bugs exposed during the refactor.\n\nCocoon lifts RegisterCustomEditor and six shared provider/registry maps (CustomEditorProviders, TreeDataProviders, WebviewViewProviders, WebviewPanels) from the ~2500-line Namespace.ts into dedicated RegisterCustomEditor.ts and Registry.ts modules. Namespace.ts shrinks by ~170 lines and re-exports through the existing path, preserving all registration behaviour unchanged.\n\nMountain extracts the 1400-line `process_mountain_request` and 600-line `send_mountain_notification` match blocks from CocoonService/mod.rs into GenericRequest::Dispatcher and GenericNotification::Dispatcher modules, reducing mod.rs by ~1900 lines. Three fixes accompany the structural extraction: scope the MutexGuard on WorkspaceFolders to a block so it is dropped before await (restoring Send for `tauri::async_runtime::spawn`); replace a permanent-None OnceLock with a two-phase RESOLVED/RETRY system that retries log resolution after Tauri creates the app-data directory; and replace a bare `return Ok(...)` inside a WindServiceHandlers match arm that broke `Scheduler::Submit`'s `Output = ()` bound with an if/else expression. A clippy-nit removing redundant `.as_str()` in AliasPath.rs is included, and two follow-up commits normalize dispatcher indentation and update dev-profile build identifiers.\n\nWorker normalises indentation across all three ESBuild config files to hard tabs across two style-only commits. Zero functional changes — build output is identical.\n\nThe structural decompositions reduce module surface area across all three components, and the runtime fixes correct latent concurrency, deferred-resolution, and control-flow bugs in Mountain.",
			"SHA": "35ece0fa0ff4a2d343c635caa89af1b4f18d825c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:38:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Advance Element submodule with Cocoon decomposition, hierarchy RPC, and IPC fixes\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to 3e397f73, pulling in a coordinated commit spanning Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky that decomposes the extension host monolith, wires call/type hierarchy RPC, and fixes data accuracy across the IPC pipeline.\n\nCocoon splits the ~1500-line inline extension host handler into three focused modules (VscodeModuleHooks, EnsureVscodeAPI, ActivateExtension) and fixes five real-world extension compatibility issues: Copilot dist-preflight failure, `context.extension.packageJSON` populated from the real manifest, workspace config cache seeded from `contributes.configuration.properties` before activation, `activate()` return value backfilled into the registry, and a POJO-tolerant RelativePattern wrapper for Shopify.ruby-lsp. Six missing VS Code API enums (LogLevel, OverviewRulerLane, UIKind, TextEditorCursorStyle, DebugConfigurationProviderTriggerKind, IndentAction) are now defined.\n\nMountain adds language-scoped configuration overrides for per-language formatter support, a OnceLock-backed static session ID for consistent telemetry, and dispatches `$provideCallHierarchyItems`/`$provideTypeHierarchyItems` RPC endpoints unblocking call/type hierarchy in the editor. Three `mountain_*` IPC stubs return real data, SOCKS proxy env-var parsing emits the correct PAC keyword, and the `didChangeTextEditorSelection` Vine notification now includes accurate `viewColumn` from split-editor layouts.\n\nSky replaces the hardcoded `viewColumn: 1` in editor IPC payloads with a `GetViewColumn()` helper reading `EditorGroups.activeGroup.index` and converting to the 1-based view column expected by the VS Code API.\n\nExtension host reliability and IPC data accuracy are materially improved across all three layers of the round-trip.",
			"SHA": "6ccd9cba20f3630bfb390502807d9b17accd94b0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:22:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Advance Element submodule with save notifications, IPC hardening, and Sky bridge decomposition\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to 21c3681b, pulling in two coordinated commits spanning Mountain, Cocoon, and Sky.\n\nMountain fires $acceptModelSaved via Vine after disk writes in FileWriteNative and TextfileWrite, enabling Cocoon to dispatch onDidSaveTextDocument to format-on-save and organize-imports extensions. On macOS, Undo/Redo is removed from the native Edit submenu via AppMenu::SetAppMenu so Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z reach Monaco's keydown handler instead of AppKit's responder chain. File write handlers now propagate configuration.change notifications to invalidate Cocoon's ConfigCache. A StorageWriteDebouncer race is fixed by reordering the flush loop, and boot latency is reduced by removing a 3-second blocking WaitForClientConnection from language handlers.\n\nCocoon replaces stale/empty state placeholders with live-tracking counterparts: __visibleTextEditors is upserted on selection changes and filtered on model removal, terminals are tracked with proper dispose cleanup, and a module-level _AllDiagnostics cache mirrors every DiagnosticCollection call with didChange event emission.\n\nSky decomposes ~2500 lines of inline handler registrations in Bridge.ts into four dedicated modules via dynamic imports — InstallWebview.ts, InstallEditorOperations.ts, InstallTreeView.ts (with exponential backoff retry), and InstallUiRequests.ts — each receiving only required dependencies through a thin injector interface.\n\nMaintain regenerates rustdoc output against Rust nightly 1.97.0.",
			"SHA": "69fc21edf6ba430415e91ed6e74b3fdf2cf8da23"
		}
	],
